records.instructions:
1. Work on concept2cure-v2 only (merge, never rebase). Red first: add tests/db/vault-version-restore.dbtest.ts. It checks in v1 then v2, then POSTs a restore of v1 with a reason and expects v3 with v1's content_hash, superseding v2. At HEAD the route 404s, and re-uploading v1's bytes with supersedesDocumentId returns 409 CONTENT_ALREADY_A_VERSION (vault-version-checkin.ts:171-184).
2. In server/services/vault/vault-version-checkin.ts, add planRestore(q, {organizationId, programId, headId, sourceVersionId, lock}). Reuse planCheckIn's head lookup, currency, link-conflict and nextMajorVersion checks, and skip the known-bytes refusal only for the source version's own hash. The source must be a live member of the same family under vault-version-family.ts VALID_LINK.
3. In server/services/vault/vault-ingest.service.ts, add restoreVaultVersion(). In one transaction, with FOR UPDATE on the head (as at :266) and the assertVaultWrite authority check from vault-write-authority.ts, it:
   - inserts the new row with the next major version, supersedes_id = head, and content_hash = the source's hash;
   - copies the source object to a new storage key, so the row stays write-once under migrations/20260926_vault_documents_record_immutability.sql and the VR-06 rules;
   - writes a chained audit event 'vault.version.restored' with {sourceVersionId, reason}.
4. In server/routes/c2c/project-vault.ts, add POST '/:id/documents/:documentId/versions/:versionId/restore' next to GET versions (:1647), behind requireEditorAccess. The body is {reason: string, at least 10 characters}. Return planRestore's 404 and 409 refusals verbatim.
5. Check-out:
   - add a new IF NOT EXISTS-guarded migration in C2C_MIGRATION_FILES, before the final sweep pair (ci:migration-set-order). It creates public.vault_document_checkouts (id uuid pk, organization_id INTEGER NOT NULL, program_id uuid NOT NULL, document_code text NOT NULL, checked_out_by int NOT NULL, checked_out_at timestamptz default now(), expires_at timestamptz NOT NULL, reason text, UNIQUE (organization_id, program_id, document_code)), so the tenant sweep gives it RLS;
   - add POST and DELETE '/:id/documents/:documentId/checkout' with audit rows, following the DurableLockManager pattern over collab_section_locks (server/routes/realtime-collab.ts:777+);
   - planCheckIn and planRestore refuse with 409 DOCUMENT_CHECKED_OUT, naming the holder and expiry, when another user holds an unexpired check-out. A manager can override with a reason, and the override is audited.
6. In client/src/concept2cure/v2/surfaces/VaultVersions.tsx:
   - add 'Restore as new version' with a reason prompt on non-current versions;
   - add 'Check out' and 'Cancel check-out', and show the holder;
   - disable 'Upload new version' (:385-394) for other users while the document is checked out.
7. Verify every gate by making it fail first: restore by a viewer gets 403; restore of another program's version gets 404; a check-in by user B during A's check-out gets 409.
